# =============================================================================
# Repo slimmed to the CANONICAL K5 QPSK Jupiter modem design. Everything at repo
# root is IGNORED except the keepers whitelisted below; the ~150 experimental
# snapshot dirs (composite_*, V*, fec_*, zed_*, jupiter_t8*, rf_*, ...) remain on
# LOCAL DISK, untracked -- they are NOT in the repo. Re-add one with:
#     git add -f <path>
#
# 2026-09-25: this file had been commented out in its ENTIRETY (0 active lines),
# so `git status` listed every build artifact and every capture directory. That
# noise is why host/qpsk_fec.{c,h} sat untracked and unnoticed even though
# ops/provision.sh scp's and compiles them -- a fresh clone could not provision.
# Restored, and the whitelist below is now generated from the set of top-level
# paths git actually tracks (it had drifted: /host/ and /images/ were missing).
#
# NOTE ON THE ARTIFACT PATTERNS BELOW (*.log, *.out, docs/superpowers/): 212
# TRACKED evidence files match them (181 .log, 20 .md under docs/superpowers/,
# 9 .out, 2 .txt -- measured with `git ls-files -z | git check-ignore --stdin -z
# --no-index`). That is harmless: .gitignore does not apply to files git already
# tracks, so they still diff, commit and clone normally, and no .c/.h/.sh source
# is among them. It does mean `git clean -x` would delete them -- `git clean -n`
# first. Re-run that pipeline after editing the patterns below.
# =============================================================================

# ---- ignore all root entries, then whitelist the canonical keepers ----
/*
!/2026-07-01-bidir-240k-k5-design.md
!/boot_known_good/
!/build_env_jupiter.sh
!/contract/
!/docs/
!/docs_session/
!/evm/
!/.gitignore
!/host/
!/host_app_k5/
!/images/
!/ip_error_fix.md
!/issue1.md
!/jupiter_240k5_byte/
!/jupiter_byte_ddrcap2_build/
!/jupiter_byte_txfix_fetch.sh
!/jupiter_byte_txfix_kit.sh
!/k5_240/
!/kill_watchdogs.md
!/modem/
!/ops/
!/OVERNIGHT_LOG.md
!/plans/
!/README.md
!/REPRODUCE.md
!/tests/
!/tick_repro/
!/tick_repro_r3/
!/tools/
!/two_jup/

# ---- build/derived artifacts INSIDE the kept dirs. These come AFTER the
#      whitelist re-includes so they win (last matching pattern decides). ----
*.iq
*.mat
# golden payloads are load-bearing (loaded by the build gates) -- keep despite *.mat
!/k5_240/golden_k5.mat
!/k5_240/golden_f1536.mat
!/contract/golden_k5.mat
!/contract/golden_f1536.mat
*.log
*.out
*.jou
*.pyc
*.vvp
*.vvpout
*.autosave
*BOOT.BIN
*BOOT.BIN.save
hdl_prj_*/
slprj/
obj_*/
.Xil/
ipcore/
s1_rtl/
__pycache__/
docs/superpowers/
two_jup/phaseB_agc/
jupiter_240k5_byte/rtl_sim/*.txt
jupiter_240k5_byte/rtl_sim/*.csv
jupiter_240k5_byte/rtl_sim/diag/
jupiter_240k5_byte/rtl_sim/replay/
two_jup/hunt/
two_jup/paired/
two_jup/census/
host_app_k5/qpsk_tun
host_app_k5/qpsk_capture
host_app_k5/qpsk_ringwrite
host_app_k5/test_frame
host_app_k5/test_k5
host_app_k5/test_ber
host_app_k5/test_whiten
host_app_k5/test_seq

# ---- added 2026-09-25 ----
# The UIO kernel is banked COMPRESSED (Image.*-uio.*.gz, tracked, 14M). Unpacking
# it leaves a 47M byte-identical copy beside it; that copy is derived, never commit it.
/images/Image.*-uio.*
!/images/Image.*-uio.*.gz
# r3 capture output written by two_jup/capture_r3.sh restore runs.
two_jup/r3cap/restore_*/
